  <refbody>
    <section id="slice-shapes">
      <title>Slice shapes</title>
      <note conref="../reuse/tpu-warehouse.dita#tpu-warehouse/note-slice-shape"/>
      <table outputclass="slice-shapes">
        <tgroup cols="6">
          <colspec colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colname="c3"/>
          <colspec colname="c4"/>
          <colspec colname="c5"/>
          <colspec colname="c6"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>slice shape</entry>
              <entry>number of chips</entry>
              <entry>number of hosts</entry>
              <entry>number of VMs</entry>
              <entry>number of cubes</entry>
              <entry>scope</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>2x2x1</entry>
              <entry>4</entry>
              <entry>1</entry>
              <entry>1</entry>
              <entry>1/16</entry>
              <entry>Single-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>2x2x2</entry>
              <entry>8</entry>
              <entry>2</entry>
              <entry>2</entry>
              <entry>1/8</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>2x2x4</entry>
              <entry>16</entry>
              <entry>4</entry>
              <entry>4</entry>
              <entry>1/4</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>2x4x4</entry>
              <entry>32</entry>
              <entry>8</entry>
              <entry>8</entry>
              <entry>1/2</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>4x4x4</entry>
              <entry>64</entry>
              <entry>16</entry>
              <entry>16</entry>
              <entry>1</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>4x4x8</entry>
              <entry>128</entry>
              <entry>32</entry>
              <entry>32</entry>
              <entry>2</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>4x8x8</entry>
              <entry>256</entry>
              <entry>64</entry>
              <entry>64</entry>
              <entry>4</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>8x8x8</entry>
              <entry>512</entry>
              <entry>128</entry>
              <entry>128</entry>
              <entry>8</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>8x8x16</entry>
              <entry>1024</entry>
              <entry>256</entry>
              <entry>256</entry>
              <entry>16</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>8x16x16</entry>
              <entry>2048</entry>
              <entry>512</entry>
              <entry>512</entry>
              <entry>32</entry>
              <entry>Multi-host</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <p>Slice shapes take the form <codeph>AxBxC</codeph>; each dimension is a multiple of 4, up to <keyword keyref="tpu7x-chips-per-pod"/> chips.</p>
      <p>Every slice shape uses the <keyword keyref="tpu7x-machine-type"/> machine type with <keyword keyref="tpu7x-chips-per-vm"/> chips.</p>
      <p>Slices larger than <keyword keyref="tpu7x-max-api-slice"/> chips need a request to the account team.</p>
    </section>
  </refbody>
</reference>
